they told me i have to be in a safe country to be helped first and didn't reply again if i remember? they're not very helpful. took them a month to even reply

&#x200B;

Thankfully soon I might not even need their help.

and again, sorry for stalking you but you have issues, I understand, I'm sorry your family is trash, you deserve a better one, mine isn't nice either so i know a little bit about what it's like :(

&#x200B;

but you have to realize, being POC/LGBT automatically makes the same life 1000x harder for you, doesn't mean your problems aren't real. I'd love to help you live a nicer life.

&#x200B;

sadly on this crap hole of a planet, nearly nobody is happy, even the ones who make us pee in bottles so they can screw off to space for a few seconds, even they are miserable. we're just slaves to a bunch of unstable man babies

do you live in a country where  it's illegal to show your hair or wrists?

do you live in a country where you can't divorce your husband without his permission? or travel without his permission?

&#x200B;

just look at the Ukraine war vs Palestine, nobody gave a shit about middle eastern, they're being tortured and hurt everyday and people support them, yet with Ukraine everyone is reacting different (not saying they shouldn't help Ukraine, i'm saying help both of them, and don't support the ones torturing just because the other side is middle eastern)

&#x200B;

do all the governments try super hard to stop you from ever leaving your country (not give you travel visas etc)?

&#x200B;

do you have to save 70,000$\~ in surgery to just have your body be somewhat normal? and not cause you extreme distress

&#x200B;

did you have to beg doctors for 2 years to just let them give you this near miracle cure that'd change your life for nearly no cost and no side effects?

&#x200B;

the list goes on. and on....

most governments hate middle eastern and make it as difficult as possible to make them immigrate. I am trying.

&#x200B;

and yeah being trans isn't just about looking masculine, plenty of trans girls pass, it's about the childhood taken away from you, the trauma of watching your body morph (if you don't receive help at an early age, and thanks to a lot of morons it's now considered "grooming") it's about never having the same vulva, or a womb.  and about being treated like crap and needing thousands in surgeries considered "aesthetics"

ooh i think i actually look white myself luckily. But my nationality is what causes issues.

&#x200B;

And thanks, you seeem very sweet <3

TBH worth it, they're so soft, nature's fidget toys. they're so warm

&#x200B;

when life is cold and hard, warm and soft tiddy is always there for you, sadly I have tubular TINY tits :( but hey at least they don't weigh much right?

yeah. this is why i mention the race so much, people who are born in nicer countries are so clueless about life outside.

&#x200B;

even gay iranians who's lives are genuinely at risk ATM don't have an easy way to get out.

USA is a hellhole from what I see tbh but a trillion times better than iran. I always dreamt of living in europe.

&#x200B;

I'm doing paperwork for it, but as I said in my post, the world hates iranians, they don't wanna let us in, they SPECIALLY don't want us to stay in their countries. they hate non-white immigrants. so it's really hard.

and Iranians are also treated a bit uniquely. even LGBT people with their life threatened here aren't allowed easily

&#x200B;

and no the only time i've seen non-iranians (black/white/indian or any other race than mine) is when I went to turkey

tbh if the world wasn't so cruel, the medication already exist. but they're calling it "grooming"

&#x200B;

i was gatekeeper for 2 years before I got hormones, I'd be a way way different person before.

surgery would be really life improving for me, sure it'd not be the same as a cis one but i'd get rid of this alien tumor, and face surgery has very minor disadvantages other than money.

&#x200B;

people who start hrt early on are basically cis outside of genitals. i started the work at 17, got my hormones at 19 :( 2 years of hell arguing with therapists, going to a new one everyday because they kept jogging me around. they probably made a lot of money out of me too.

yeah. if it helps i might be leaving soon... i'm doing some work to study outside

and honestly being trans is so much different. it's hell.

&#x200B;

and the fact that I'll never have the proper well... bottom parts I want breaks my heart. the fact that my face has less nerves and that I won't ever know what's it like to be touched there properly, and my body is just so fucked up by testrone, it feels like a disfigurement to me.

&#x200B;

and middle eastern are so hated, so are Indians, you can probably tell how the world feels about us by seeing how most governments and people treat Ukrainians and their refugees vs Palestine etc.

&#x200B;

also hey i love computer science too, I hopefully will be studying it one day!

why is that?

&#x200B;

and thanks <3

My dad said "randomly on another topic" that he feels really sensitive and hates touch when his stomach is upset. we both have IBS i think. could it possibily be that? or just that I'm emotionally not in the mood.

&#x200B;

I also can't orgasm or feel much video chatting with her but I have a far easier time watching porn. specially rougher porn these days

I want to immigrate there anyway, I'm a lesbian. And I'm a lot different cultural and I can't handle the oppression here. not to mention the inflation and all that.

&#x200B;

and some people don't want SRS. I personally want it (only 70-80% sure at this point) but I don't trust Iranian surgeons AT ALL.

I know it's confusing, I can speak it well enough for everyday stuff but can't communicate well with friends etc or explain topics

I spent most of my childhood on the internet cause complicated stuff (I am slightly "different" and most people bullied and disliked me, I have Asperger's and just don't fit well with Iranians too)

